The Vault of Whispers is a pre-Galifaran arcane repository believed to contain dozens of bound extraplanar entities — elementals, daelkyr-adjacent horrors, and at least one entity described only as "the First Voice." Its location is unconfirmed but most evidence points to the interior of [[The Mournland]].

!! Origins
The Vault predates Galifar by at least three centuries. Fragmentary records in the Korranberg Chronicle and certain [[House Cannith]] deep archives reference a "Chamber of Bound Voices" built by pre-war artificers and binding specialists under an unnamed Cyran noble house. The builders appear to have been deliberately erased from the historical record.

!! What Is Inside
According to contradictory sources, the Vault contains:
* Multiple bound entities, each imprisoned in a separate whisper chamber with its own sealing mechanism
* A range of entity types: elementals, entities associated with Xoriat and the Daelkyr, and "the First Voice"
* A master control mechanism built into the Vault's architecture, intended to keep all seals permanent

The Day of Mourning may have damaged the seals. If any bound entity has been freed, the threat is of unknown magnitude.

!! The Whisper Connection
[[The Whisper]] shares the Vault's name — whether by coincidence, design, or because they are somehow connected to it is the campaign's central question.

!! Connections
* [[The Mournland]] (believed location)
* [[The Whisper]] (possible connection)
* [[Lady Elaydren d'Cannith]] (seeks something inside)
